<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">31 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 31 March, from 1146 to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/damascus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/damascus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1146 CE <span class="tih-ago">880 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bernard of Clairvaux preaches the Second Crusade at Vézelay</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bernard's sermon on a hillside at Vézelay moved Louis VII and crowds of nobles to take the cross after the fall of Edessa. The crusade ended in failure before Damascus in 1148.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1492 CE <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ferdinand and Isabella order the expulsion of Spain's Jews</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Alhambra Decree gave Jews four months to convert or leave. Tens of thousands left, and Sephardic communities took root in the Ottoman Empire, North Africa and the Low Countries.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1596 CE <span class="tih-ago">430 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">René Descartes is born in Touraine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The philosopher and mathematician sought certainty through doubt, concluding 'I think, therefore I am'. He also devised the coordinate geometry that links algebra and geometry.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1889 CE <span class="tih-ago">137 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gustave Eiffel inaugurates his tower in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Eiffel climbed the stairs of his newly completed tower to raise the French flag for the Exposition Universelle. At 300 metres it was the tallest structure in the world until 1930.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1917 CE <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">United States takes possession of the Danish West Indies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Denmark transferred St Thomas, St John and St Croix, sold for 25 million dollars in gold. The US wanted to deny the islands to Germany and guard the approaches to the Panama Canal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1968 CE <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lyndon B. Johnson says he will not seek re-election</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a televised address on Vietnam, Johnson announced a partial bombing halt and said he would not run again. Richard Nixon won the presidency that November.</p></div></li></ol>
